      ],
      "summary": "A link to a suite installs nothing by itself: `desktop.join(suite, { source })` shows the person an install sheet with each application's origin, the contracts it offers, the scopes it asks for (each a choice) and the assistant's access (off), and installs only what they add, kept in their state. An application joined before is updated without asking unless it now comes from another origin or asks for more. An application on this device or the local network says that the browser may ask about it, and its window says how to recover when that was refused. Settings has a section of the desktop's own, Applications and access: every application's origin, grants and recent calls, with switches for the scopes and the assistant's access of the ones the person added, and Remove. The Pages desktop joins `?suite=` links this way.",
      "id": "install-sheet"
    },
